  "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.7925$ lies between. These numbers are $0.7910$ and $0.7939.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.7910 & <0.7925<0.7939\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.81) & <Φ(z)<Φ(0.82).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{0.81+0.82}{2}=0.815.\n$$",
